@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Context
+
+Tasks are stored in a `Map` keyed by title in `createTaskList`. See proposal.md - Why. The domain cannot use clock or randomness, so the id must be generated deterministically.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+- Goals: stable unique ids, lookup by id, id-or-title in existing operations.
+- Non-Goals: persistence of ids, caller-supplied ids, changing title uniqueness.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Counter ids**: each list holds a counter; `add` assigns `task-<n>` (n from 1, never reused, even after remove). Alternatives: random/UUID (forbidden in the domain), caller-passed id (changes `add`'s input and the app's screens).
+- **`createTask` takes the id as a second parameter**, keeping `task.ts` pure.
+- **Id index**: a second `Map<string, string>` is unnecessary; keep tasks in a `Map` keyed by id and resolve titles by scanning, or keep the title map plus an id→title map. Chosen: keep title map and add an id→title map updated on rename/remove.
+- **Resolution order**: text matching an id wins, then title. A task titled like another task's id (e.g. "task-2") is therefore reachable by title only when no task has that id. Accepted trade-off.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Title that looks like an id is shadowed] → id match first; documented.
+- [Existing test comparing whole task] → update it to include the id.
