@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+## Why
+
+The app can only refer to a task by its title, and a title changes when the task is renamed. Each task needs a stable identifier that survives renames.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets an `id`: a string no other task of the list has, kept when the task is renamed, completed, tagged, etc.
+- `add` returns the task with its `id`.
+- New `get(id)` on the list returns the task with that id as a `Result` (`not-found` when there is none).
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept a task's id as well as its title.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-identity`: tasks have a stable unique id, lookup by id, and id accepted wherever a title identifies a task.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None (no accepted specs exist yet).
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts`: `Task` gains `id`; `createTask` takes the id from its caller.
+- `src/domain/list.ts`: id generation (a per-list counter), id index, `get`, id-or-title lookup.
+- `src/index.ts`: no new export; `Task` and `TaskList` are already exported and gain the field and method. The public API changes.
+- Tests in `test/list.test.ts`; the existing `add` test compares a whole task and must include the id.
+
+## Project rules
+
+- No wall clock or randomness in the domain: ids come from a deterministic counter held by the list, not from `Date.now()` or `Math.random()`.
+- Errors as `Result`: `get` and id lookups return `not-found`, never throw.
+- TSDoc on every exported function, including any new one; no new runtime dependency.
